atom     unicode/chrs-negative-codepoint
source   curated
kind     output validity — the answer is not merely wrong, it is not text

# Found by the method matrix: rakupp answers `(-1).chrs` with the bytes
# ff bf bf bf, which are not valid UTF-8. Storing that observation put an
# undecodable byte sequence into five .grid files and broke every command that
# reads the suite — one cell, whole tool down.
#
# A negative number is not a codepoint. Rakudo says so; rakupp encodes -1 as
# though it were one and emits the result.

- id     0001
  from   generator:gen/methods.raku · review:2026-08-16
  code   (-1).chrs
  throws X::AdHoc
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → ERR:X::AdHoc
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-77-gf431f48-dirty → INVALID-UTF8: ff bf bf bf

- id     0002
  from   review:2026-08-16
  code   (-1).chr
  throws X::AdHoc
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → ERR:X::AdHoc

- id     0003
  from   review:2026-08-16 · the boundary the reference states
  code   (0x110000).chr
  throws X::AdHoc
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → ERR:X::AdHoc
